A func written in a platform override body is that body's helper, on the same
terms as a var or a type it declares (#230). The override's own body calls it,
and a component nested in that body reaches it through lookupBodyMethod's
owner chain -- the capture route a method takes, since a component-body func
is a method on its owner rather than a name in scope.

Both overrides declare `bump`, and neither is a redeclaration of the other:
each override body gets its own clone of the component's method table, and
specializeComp swaps the whole list, so a build only ever holds the target's
own. Two platform packages implementing one component must not have to agree
on their helpers' names.

`fromBase` is what the override *inherits*: the clone starts from the base
declaration's table, so a helper the declaration wrote stays callable from an
override that did not rewrite it.

What this pins is the ir.Body half again. Component.Funcs and Component.Methods
are restored to the base's when checkPendingExtensions finishes, so the
override's helper survives to lowering only by travelling in the override's own
ir.Body and being swapped back by specializeComp. Without that swap the call
reaches each backend with no declaration emitted for it.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `htmlTally` -- guards specializeComp's pre-existing Vars swap, not this fixture's subject: it holds if that swap ever becomes a merge, and the Funcs/Methods swap can be removed without either of these two firing
deny out/none/html/index.html `btTally` -- the same claim from the other target
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `\(m \*outer\)` -- the helper is cloned onto the model, so no method is emitted on the component's own name; without the ir.Body swap bubbletea wrote `func (m *outer) Bump()` against a type it never declares
deny out/none/html/index.html `outer_bump\(` -- the same from html's side: only the per-instance clone is emitted, so the un-instanced name appears in neither the declaration nor a call
deny * `\blabel\b` -- the captured prop is substituted by the instantiation's argument, so no target emits its name

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import "sngl:platform/html"
import "sngl:platform/bubbletea"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
}

component outer(label = "") node {
    var base = 1

    func fromBase() => base + 1

    text(value="plain {label} {fromBase()}")
}

component outer[html.platform] {
    var htmlTally = 0

    func bump() { htmlTally = htmlTally + 100 }

    component inner(step = 1) node {
        var runs = 0

        vbox {
            text(value="{label} {htmlTally} {runs} {fromBase()}")
            button(text="+", @click {
                htmlTally = htmlTally + step
                runs = runs + 1
                bump()
            })
        }
    }

    vbox {
        inner(step=1)
        inner(step=10)
    }
}

component outer[bubbletea.platform] {
    var btTally = 0

    func bump() { btTally = btTally + 100 }

    component inner(step = 1) node {
        var runs = 0

        vbox {
            text(value="{label} {btTally} {runs} {fromBase()}")
            button(text="+", @click {
                btTally = btTally + step
                runs = runs + 1
                bump()
            })
        }
    }

    vbox {
        inner(step=1)
        inner(step=10)
    }
}

window {
    outer(label="L")
}
